+# ACP Subagent Grouping & Virtual Transcripts
+
+**Date:** 2026-06-23
+**Status:** Approved design, ready for implementation planning
+**Target repo:** Zed submodule (`zed/`), branch `feature/acp-subagent-grouping` off `zedium-applied`
+
+## Problem
+
+When an external ACP provider runs a subagent, its activity currently lands flat in the
+single main transcript of the agent panel, and there is no way to open the subagent's
+separate transcript. Zed's *native* agent already has a rich subagent experience (a
+collapsible card with a live preview and a pop-out to the full child transcript), but that
+machinery is wired exclusively to the native agent and never fires for external ACP
+providers.
+
+### Why the native path doesn't generalize (verified on the wire)
+
+The native subagent UI is triggered by two native-only signals:
+
+1. A Zed-private meta key `SUBAGENT_SESSION_INFO_META_KEY` (carrying
+   `SubagentSessionInfo { session_id, message_start_index, message_end_index }`) attached
+   to the spawn tool call. Written **only** in `crates/agent/src/tools/spawn_agent_tool.rs`.
+2. The `AcpThreadEvent::SubagentSpawned` event, emitted **only** from the native path,
+   which drives `ConversationView::load_subagent_session` to open the child as a separate
+   loadable ACP session (`connection.load_session(subagent_id, ...)`).
+
+External ACP providers emit neither, so `ToolCall::is_subagent()` is false and every
+subagent step renders flat.
+
+### How qwen-code actually expresses subagents (observed live)
+
+Captured by driving `qwen --acp` (v0.19.1) with a subagent-forcing prompt
+(`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-qwen-acp-wire-capture.log`). Findings:
+
+- **Single ACP session.** No `session/new` for the subagent — everything stays on one
+  `sessionId`. (qwen declares `loadSession: true` capability, but does *not* create a
+  child session for subagents.)
+- **Subagent invocation = an ordinary tool call** with
+  `_meta: { toolName: "agent", provenance: "builtin" }`. Its final `content` is the
+  subagent's summary text.
+- **Each subagent step = an ordinary top-level `session/update` tool call** on the *same*
+  session, tagged:
+  ```json
+  "_meta": { "toolName": "read_file", "provenance": "subagent",
+             "subagentType": "Explore", "parentToolCallId": "call_4ca2…" }
+  ```
+
+So qwen gives a **parent-pointer tree** (`parentToolCallId` + `provenance` +
+`subagentType`), not nested sessions. Native gives a separate session + index range. Two
+incompatible wire shapes, both via `_meta`, no standardization.
+
+| | Zed native | qwen-code |
+|---|---|---|
+| Subagent identity | separate ACP session | an "agent" tool call on the same session |
+| Child steps | entries in the child session | flat tool calls tagged `parentToolCallId` |
+| Linking metadata | `subagent_session_info` (start/end index) | `parentToolCallId` / `provenance` / `subagentType` |
+
+## Goal
+
+Bring external ACP providers (qwen-code first) up to the **card + live-preview + pop-out**
+experience native already has, via a generalized grouping abstraction in `acp_thread` that
+can ingest either wire shape, with a clean per-provider extension seam. No regression for
+providers without an adapter.
+
+## Approved decisions (from brainstorming)
+
+1. **Surface shape:** card + live preview + pop-out (parity with native).
+2. **Pop-out realization:** a **virtual grouped view** — a read-only sub-transcript
+   reconstructed by filtering the parent `AcpThread`'s entries to the subagent's subtree.
+   No backend/child session required. Reuses the existing `ThreadView` renderer.
+3. **Generality:** **built-in per-provider adapters** behind a `SubagentGrouping` trait —
+   one impl reads native's `subagent_session_info`, one reads qwen's
+   `parentToolCallId`/`provenance`/`subagentType`. Adding a provider = a localized new impl.
+4. **Nesting:** **recursive true tree** — a subagent card can contain another subagent
+   card, each independently collapsible and pop-out-able, with a breadcrumb chain.
+
+## Design
+
+### 1. Normalized model (`crates/acp_thread`)
+
+Normalize every provider's wire shape to one internal representation. For each tool call we
+derive a membership (stored as a side-index on `AcpThread`, keyed by `acp::ToolCallId`, to
+avoid widening `ToolCall` for non-subagent providers):
+
+```rust
+struct SubagentMembership {
+    root: acp::ToolCallId,            // the spawn/"agent" tool call owning the subtree
+    parent: Option<acp::ToolCallId>,  // immediate parent (= root unless deeper nesting)
+    subagent_type: SharedString,      // "Explore" — the card title
+    depth: u8,
+}
+```
+
+The grouping is a real tree: a member's `parent` may itself be a group root. A tool call
+with no membership is a normal top-level entry. A group root is a tool call that owns a
+subtree (identified by the adapter's `is_root`).
+
+`AcpThread` gains a `SubagentIndex` holding:
+- `roots: IndexMap<ToolCallId, SubagentGroup>` (label, status mirror, ordered child ids)
+- `membership: HashMap<ToolCallId, SubagentMembership>`
+- helper queries: `is_subagent_root`, `membership_of`, `subtree_entries(root)` (recursive,
+  returns the slice of `AgentThreadEntry` indices belonging to a root, depth-first).
+
+### 2. Extension seam — `SubagentGrouping` trait
+
+```rust
+pub trait SubagentGrouping {
+    /// Is this tool call itself a subagent root (a spawn)? Returns the display label.
+    fn root_label(&self, tool_call: &acp::ToolCall) -> Option<SharedString>;
+    /// Classify a tool call as a member of some root's subtree.
+    fn classify(&self, tool_call: &acp::ToolCall, index: &SubagentIndex)
+        -> Option<SubagentMembership>;
+}
+```
+
+Impls (in `crates/acp_thread` or alongside each connection):
+- `NativeSubagentGrouping` — reads `subagent_session_info` meta (already parsed today).
+- `QwenSubagentGrouping` — `root_label` matches `_meta.toolName == "agent"` (label from
+  the spawned `subagentType` of its children, or the tool title); `classify` reads
+  `_meta.parentToolCallId` + `provenance == "subagent"` + `subagentType`, resolving `depth`
+  by walking `parentToolCallId` to the root.
+
+Selected per connection via a new method on the existing `AgentConnection` trait
+(`crates/acp_thread/src/connection.rs`):
+
+```rust
+fn subagent_grouping(&self) -> Option<Rc<dyn SubagentGrouping>> { None }
+```
+
+- `NativeAgentConnection` returns `NativeSubagentGrouping`.
+- `AcpConnection` (`crates/agent_servers/src/acp.rs`) returns an adapter chosen from the
+  agent's reported `agentInfo.name` (e.g. `"qwen-code"` → `QwenSubagentGrouping`).
+- Unknown providers → `None` → today's flat behavior, **zero regression**.
+
+This trait + the `subagent_grouping()` connection method is the concrete "extension point
+for ACP providers" the exploration set out to find.
+
+### 3. Ingest wiring (`AcpThread::handle_session_update`)
+
+Tool-call meta is already parsed in `ToolCall::from_acp`. After a tool call is
+upserted/updated:
+1. If `grouping.root_label(tc)` is `Some`, register/refresh a `SubagentGroup` root.
+2. Else if `grouping.classify(tc, index)` is `Some`, record membership and append to the
+   root's ordered child list.
+
+Robustness (matches observed wire realities):
+- **Out-of-order:** a child may arrive before or after its root. Membership resolves
+  lazily by walking the `parentToolCallId` map; ordering is irrelevant. Late-arriving roots
+  retroactively claim already-seen orphans.
+- **Orphans** (parent id never resolves): rendered normally in the main list, never dropped.
+- **No adapter:** index stays empty; rendering is unchanged.
+
+### 4. Rendering (`crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs`)
+
+- `render_entry` / `render_any_tool_call`: a tool call that is a **member** of any subtree
+  is **skipped** in the main flat list (this removes the pollution). A **group root**
+  renders the subagent **card**.
+- Generalize the existing `render_subagent_card` to be driven by the normalized
+  `SubagentGroup`/`SubagentIndex` instead of `subagent_session_info` + a loaded child
+  `ThreadView`. Card contents:
+  - `subagent_type` title, status icon (spinner / ✓ / ✗ / canceled),
+  - live tool count, file-change stats (added/removed) where derivable,
+  - the root tool call's final `content` as the summary footer,
+  - while running: the last N child entries shown live (the "preview"),
+  - a pop-out affordance (⤢).
+- **Pop-out = virtual `SubagentView`** (read-only): filters the parent `AcpThread`'s
+  entries to `subtree_entries(root)` and renders them by reusing
+  `ThreadView::render_entry`. Recursive nesting → nested cards, each independently
+  pop-out-able, with a breadcrumb back up the `parent` chain. Navigation reuses the
+  existing `ConnectedServerState.threads` / `navigate_to_thread` substrate, but the entry
+  is a virtual view over the parent thread rather than a loaded session.
+- The root summary lives **only** in the card/virtual view, not duplicated as a normal
+  assistant message in main, keeping the main transcript clean.
+
+### 5. Component boundaries
+
+- `acp_thread`: owns the normalized model, the `SubagentGrouping` trait, both adapters, and
+  the ingest logic. No UI dependency. Independently unit-testable.
+- `agent_servers`: selects the adapter per connection from `agentInfo.name`.
+- `agent_ui`: consumes `SubagentIndex` for rendering only; contains no
+  provider-specific knowledge.
+
+## Testing
+
+- **Fixture:** the live qwen capture
+  (`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-qwen-acp-wire-capture.log`) plus a distilled JSONL
+  of the session/update notifications. Canonical structure: root `call_4ca2…`
+  (`toolName: "agent"`) with five `Explore` children
+  (`glob`, `read_file ×4`, all `provenance: "subagent"`, `parentToolCallId: call_4ca2…`).
+- **Adapter unit tests:** feed qwen's real `_meta` sequence into `QwenSubagentGrouping`,
+  assert the resulting tree (1 root, 5 members, correct `subagent_type`, `depth`). A
+  synthetic nested case (subagent spawning a subagent) asserts recursion. Parallel test for
+  `NativeSubagentGrouping`.
+- **Ingest tests:** out-of-order arrival (child before root), orphan fallback, no-adapter
+  no-op.
+- **Render-level test:** a member tool call is absent from the main flat list and present
+  in `subtree_entries(root)`.
+
+## Out of scope (YAGNI)
+
+- A documented cross-provider subagent meta convention (deferred; per-provider adapters
+  suffice now).
+- A third-party plugin/registry rendering API.
+- Side-by-side / tabbed multi-transcript layout (pop-out + breadcrumb only).
+- Changing how native spawns subagents; we only generalize the *consumption* path.
+
+## Manual verification
+
+After implementation: run `qwen --acp` from the agent panel (already configured via
+OpenRouter on this machine), issue a subagent-forcing prompt, and confirm: (a) subagent
+steps no longer appear flat in main, (b) a card with live preview appears, (c) pop-out
+opens the recursive virtual transcript, (d) native agent subagents still work unchanged.
